            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0000\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000:F001\", \"F010\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Subsection (d)(5) provides an express governing limitation on access under this section, specifying that nothing in the section allows an individual access to information compiled in reasonable anticipation of a civil action or proceeding. Proposal P0000 properly incorporates this governing exception into the summary and context quotes to make the reading independently complete and accurate.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F001\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Proposal P0001 incorrectly asserts that the agency must require every individual, whether accompanied or unaccompanied, to furnish written authorization before access. Under the source text, furnishing a written statement authorizing discussion in an accompanying person's presence is an optional agency permission ('the agency may require') applicable specifically when an individual chooses to be accompanied.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0002\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000:F001\", \"F010\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The unchanged draft omits the governing statutory condition set forth in subsection (d)(5), which explicitly restricts access under this section for information compiled in reasonable anticipation of a civil action or proceeding. Because this governing restriction is omitted, the unchanged reading is incomplete for independent use.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
